{
  "summary": "Reject empty overflow pages as corruption when parsing read-only Berkeley DB files in BerkeleyRODatabase::Open. This prevents an infinite loop when an overflow page with zero data links back to itself or another empty page.",
  "problem": "When reading BDB overflow records, the parser terminates only when next_page is 0 or when total read bytes exceed item_len. An overflow page with no data (hf_offset of 0) adds zero bytes to the accumulator, so a cycle of empty pages causes migratewallet or bitcoin-wallet dump to spin indefinitely at 100% CPU on an HTTP worker thread and blocks node shutdown.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description measurements demonstrate bitcoin-wallet dump spinning at 100% of a core until killed after 60s on master when encountering an empty self-referential overflow page, whereas it fails immediately with this PR.",
    "PR description notes that running migratewallet against such a file causes the RPC to never return, leaves one HTTP worker at 100% CPU, and prevents clean shutdown (bitcoind stop did not finish after 30s)."
  ],
